<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Draksharama</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Draksharama is a temple town in the Godavari delta of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, home to the Bhimeswara temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a>, one of the five Pancharama shrines. The temple was built under the Eastern Chalukya kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vengi">Vengi</a> around the 9th and 10th centuries and carries hundreds of inscriptions in Telugu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/draksharama.jpg" alt="Draksharama" width="320" height="149" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aditya Gopal · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Draksharama_temple,_Draksharamam.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
